    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <div class="chart-title">Where the extra {{ n.growth_total | fm }} comes from</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">2027 forecast minus 2026 estimate, by café</div>
      {{ svg.growth }}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Parakeet Cafe · 2027 Sales Forecast</span><span>Forecasts by café and model: outputs/forecast_by_store_month.csv</span><span class="pn"></span></div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= RISKS #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="head"><img src="assets/logo-bird.png" alt="Parakeet Cafe"><span class="eyebrow">Risks &amp; assumptions</span></div>
  <h1>What could ruffle the forecast</h1>
  <p class="lede">The models know only the past. They see no new cafés, price changes or local events, and they assume the habits of 2024–26 continue. These four things would move the 2027 number.</p>
  <div class="row" style="gap:.3in;margin-top:6px">
    <div class="col risk">
      <h3>New cafés are upside</h3>
      <div class="big">+{{ n.analog_avg | fm }}</div>
      <div class="cap">average first-year sales of a new café</div>
      <p>Manhattan Beach is set up in Toast and Studio City and Enclave in R365, but none has sales yet, so none is in the forecast. Recent openings did {% for a in n.analogs %}{{ a.store }} {{ a.first12 | fm }}{{ ", " if not loop.last else "" }}{% endfor %} in their first 12 months. Add each one, prorated by the months it trades in 2027.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col risk">
      <h3>Momentum is the big bet</h3>
      <div class="big">{{ n.slow_case | fm }}</div>
      <div class="cap">2027 if like-for-like growth cools to +8%</div>
      <p>All three models extend like-for-like growth of +10%, +20% and +15% (2024–26). If 2027 growth slows to +8%, sales land near {{ n.slow_case | fm }}{% if n.slow_case < n.low %}, below the lowest model{% else %}, inside the model range{% endif %}. Track like-for-like monthly from January.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col risk">
      <h3>Growth is concentrated</h3>
      <div class="big">{{ n.top3_share | pct(0, False) }}</div>
      <div class="cap">of 2027 growth comes from three cafés</div>
      <p>{% for c in n.fast2 %}{{ c.store }} ({{ c.growth | pct }}{% if c.store == "Little Italy" %}, after a step up in March 2026{% endif %}){{ " and " if loop.first else "" }}{% endfor %} lead. If both grew +10% instead, 2027 would land near {{ n.fast2_case | fm }} ({{ (n.fast2_case / n.f2027[ENSEMBLE] - 1) | pct(1) }} vs the blend).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col risk">
      <h3>Price is an open lever</h3>
      <div class="big">{{ n.lfl[2].ticket | pct(1) }}</div>
      <div class="cap">average check, Jan–Sep 2026 vs 2025</div>
      <p>2026 growth is traffic. The average check was nearly flat at ${{ "%.2f" | format(n.lfl[2].avg_ticket) }}. The models only extend sales trends and know nothing about menu prices, so a 2027 price increase is a lever on top of this forecast, provided traffic holds.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="row" style="align-items:flex-end;margin-top:30px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.25">
      <div class="chart-title">2027 under different assumptions</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Net sales, existing 11 cafés unless stated · % vs 2026 estimate</div>
      {{ svg.scenarios }}
    </div>
    <div class="col rules" style="flex:1;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;margin:0">
      {% if P %}<div><h3>How to use it</h3>Budget at the plan, <b>{{ P.f2027 | fm }}</b>; the best estimate is {{ n.f2027[ENSEMBLE] | fm }}. For café targets each café should beat three months in four, shade café forecasts by about {{ (P.cafe_factor - 1) | pct(0) }} (single cafés miss by more). Add new cafés on top as their opening dates firm up.</div>
      {% else %}<div><h3>How to use it</h3>Budget at <b>{{ n.f2027[ENSEMBLE] | fm }}</b> (the blend), with {{ n.low_model }}'s <b>{{ n.low | fm }}</b> as the conservative case and {{ n.high_model }}'s <b>{{ n.high | fm }}</b> as the stretch. Add new cafés on top as their opening dates firm up.</div>{% endif %}
      <div><h3>Watch first</h3>Q1 2027 like-for-like against the forecast's {{ n.q1_growth | pct }}. A gap of more than 3 points is the signal to revisit.</div>
      <div><h3>Keep it fresh</h3>Re-run monthly as Toast data lands; the full pipeline (extract, back-test, forecast, this report) runs in minutes from the repo.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Parakeet Cafe · 2027 Sales Forecast</span><span>* Illustrative: half of the average first-year sales of our last four openings ({{ n.new_cafe_half_year | fm }}); opening dates are not yet set</span><span class="pn"></span></div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= APPENDIX A #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="head"><img src="assets/logo-bird.png" alt="Parakeet Cafe"><span class="eyebrow">Appendix</span></div>
  <h1>Method and data</h1>
  <div class="row small" style="margin-top:12px;gap:.32in">
    <div class="col">
      <h3>Data</h3>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Toast POS tables in the Grupo Anderson's BI warehouse, read through MCP Andersons. Net sales follow the official <i>silver.v_toast_sales_daily</i> definition: check amounts on non-voided, non-deleted checks and orders, minus Toast gift-card sales. {{ "{:,}".format(n.store_days) }} café-days ({{ n.total_sales | fm }}) from {{ n.first_day.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") }} to {{ n.last_day.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") }}, validated month by month against checksums computed in SQL.</p>
      <h3>Modelling window</h3>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Toast history starts with the Sep 2022 POS migration, so modelling starts Oct 2022. Cafés opened since then skip their 2–4 week opening ramp. Nautilus (a weekday corporate-campus café) trades Monday–Friday and closes on five holidays; the forecasts respect that calendar.</p>
      <h3>One-off disruptions</h3>
      <ul class="tight" style="margin-top:0">
      {% for line in n.anomalies %}<li>{{ line }}</li>{% endfor %}
        <li>Any other day below 25% of the café's 29-day median (partial closures)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:6px">Excluded from Prophet's training; imputed (same weekday, nearby weeks) for the monthly models; kept in the actuals used for scoring.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <h3>Prophet</h3>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Daily net sales per café: linear trend, weekly and yearly seasonality, US federal holidays plus Valentine's Day, Easter, Mother's and Father's Day, Black Friday, Christmas Eve and New Year's Eve. Monthly totals = sum of daily forecasts on trading days.</p>
      <h3>SARIMA</h3>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Monthly sales rate per café (sales ÷ trading days), seasonal ARIMA with the order chosen per café by an information criterion; orders used for 2027 are listed in the next appendix.</p>
      <h3>Holt-Winters</h3>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Same monthly rate; exponential smoothing with a trend and a 12-month seasonal pattern, parameters estimated by least squares.</p>
      <h3>Blend</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">Combines the three café by café and month by month{% if n.tuning %} ({{ "simple average" if n.tuning.blend_rule == "mean" else n.tuning.blend_rule }}){% endif %}. Settings for 2027 are on the next page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      {% if n.tuning %}{% set T = n.tuning %}
      <h3>Tuning design (round 2)</h3>
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b>Tuning set.</b> Forecasts made at the end of Sep 2024, Dec 2024, Mar 2025 and Jun 2025, scored on months 4–15 ahead that fall in 2025 ({{ T.tune_store_months }} café-months).</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b>Holdout.</b> Forecasts made at the end of Jun, Sep and Dec 2025, scored only on Jan–Sep 2026 ({{ T.holdout_store_months }} café-months), never used to choose anything.</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b>Score.</b> Average of café-month and brand-month error (WAPE), so a setting cannot win by sharpening cafés while drifting on the total.</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b>Search.</b> Prophet: {{ T.n_prophet }} Optuna (TPE) trials over nine settings and feature switches, starting from round 1. SARIMA: all {{ T.n_sarima }} combinations. Holt-Winters: all {{ T.n_hw }}.</p>
      <p style="margin:0"><b>Rules.</b> A model's tuned settings are adopted only if they lower its holdout score. The blend rule (average, median or error-weighted) is picked on the tuning set and kept only if it matches the average on the holdout.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Parakeet Cafe · 2027 Sales Forecast</span><span>Code and outputs: github.com/mre-ga/parakeet_forecasts</span><span class="pn"></span></div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= APPENDIX B #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="head"><img src="assets/logo-bird.png" alt="Parakeet Cafe"><span class="eyebrow">Appendix</span></div>
  <h1>2027 forecast by café and model</h1>
  <table style="margin-top:14px">
    <thead><tr><th class="l">Café</th><th class="l">Region</th><th>2025 actual</th><th>2026 estimate</th><th>Prophet</th><th>SARIMA</th><th>Holt-Winters</th><th>Blend</th>{% if P %}<th>Plan</th>{% endif %}<th class="l" style="padding-left:16px">SARIMA order chosen</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for c in n.cafes %}
      <tr><td>{{ c.store }}</td><td class="l muted">{{ c.region }}</td><td>{{ c.a2025 | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ c.e2026 | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ c.prophet | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ c.sarima | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ c.hw | fm(2) }}</td><td><b>{{ c.f2027 | fm(2) }}</b></td>{% if P %}<td>{{ c.plan | fm(2) }}</td>{% endif %}<td class="l muted" style="padding-left:16px">{{ c.sarima_spec }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
      <tr class="total"><td>All cafés</td><td></td><td>{{ n.a2025 | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ n.e2026 | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ n.f2027["Prophet"] | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ n.f2027["SARIMA"] | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ n.f2027["Holt-Winters"] | fm(2) }}</td><td>{{ n.f2027[ENSEMBLE] | fm(2) }}</td>{% if P %}<td>{{ P.f2027 | fm(2) }}</td>{% endif %}<td></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="row small" style="margin-top:22px;gap:.32in">
    <div class="col"><h3>Files in the repo</h3>
      <ul class="tight" style="margin-top:0">
        <li><i>data/raw/parakeet_toast_daily.csv</i>: daily net sales and checks by café</li>
        <li><i>outputs/forecast_by_store_month.csv</i>: Oct 2026 – Dec 2027 by café, month and model</li>
        <li><i>outputs/forecast_brand_month.csv</i>: brand totals with simulation ranges</li>
        <li><i>outputs/backtest_forecasts.csv</i>, <i>backtest_metrics.csv</i>: every rehearsal forecast and score</li>
      </ul></div>
    <div class="col"><h3>Reading the ranges</h3>The low–high model range is the practical planning band. Each model's own 80% interval for the 2027 total (in <i>forecast_annual.csv</i>) ranges from ±{{ n.pi_halfwidth["Prophet"] | pct(1, False) }} for Prophet to ±{{ n.pi_halfwidth["Holt-Winters"] | pct(1, False) }} for Holt-Winters. They disagree too much, and Prophet's is far tighter than its back-test misses, so we don't headline them.</div>
    <div class="col"><h3>Reproduce</h3><i>python src/backtest.py</i> → <i>python src/tune.py</i> → <i>python src/forecast_2027.py</i> → <i>python report/build_report.py</i>. Data refresh: <i>data/sql/extract_parakeet_daily.sql</i> via MCP Andersons.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Parakeet Cafe · 2027 Sales Forecast</span><span>Net sales from Toast POS · $ millions</span><span class="pn"></span></div>
</section>

{% if n.tuning %}{% set T = n.tuning %}
{# ======================================================================= APPENDIX C #}
<section class="page">
  <div class="head"><img src="assets/logo-bird.png" alt="Parakeet Cafe"><span class="eyebrow">Appendix</span></div>
  <h1>Settings: round 1 vs tuned</h1>
  <table style="margin-top:14px">
    <thead><tr><th class="l">Model</th><th class="l">Setting</th><th class="l">Best found on 2025</th><th class="l">Round 1</th><th class="l">Used for 2027</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for m in MODELS %}
      {% for label, tuned, base in T.describe_best[m] %}
      <tr class="{{ 'hl' if tuned != base else '' }}"><td>{{ m if loop.first else "" }}</td><td class="l">{{ label }}</td><td class="l">{{ tuned }}</td><td class="l muted">{{ base }}</td><td class="l">{{ tuned if T.adopted.variant[m] == "tuned" else base }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note" style="margin-top:10px">Bold rows changed. "Best found" is the top score on the 2025 tuning set; it is used for 2027 only where it also won on the 2026 holdout ({{ T.adopted_models | join(" and ") if T.adopted_models else "none" }}). Trend flexibility, seasonality and holiday strength are Prophet's prior scales: higher lets that component bend more.{% if T.blend_weights %} Blend weights: {% for m in MODELS %}{{ m }} {{ T.blend_weights[m] | pct(0, False) }}{{ ", " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}</p>
  <div class="foot"><span>Parakeet Cafe · 2027 Sales Forecast</span><span>outputs/tuned_configs.json holds the exact values</span><span class="pn"></span></div>
</section>
{% endif %}

</body>
